+The real native Throwdown Panel HUDButton is interactive (`IsPrompt=false`) and belongs to `Hud.ActivityShortcutButtonStack`, through StackScreen and the native HighlightableLabelButton. The earlier full-aspect HUD mount displayed the artwork/glyph but lacked that native shortcut focus scope. The corrected mount borrows only an empty shortcut stack and restores only its own item. Its Start action requests Activities_Details; the native activity pause flow owns phone pose, Layer_Menu and Back. The private details page uses separately exported native footer/list/anchor donors, Quit and scoreboard. The top Quit/Leave shortcut is hidden during gameplay as requested. Existing gameplay menu/marker restrictions remain enabled.
+
+The latest native dump reaches typed asset assignment at game RVA `0x3dd20ad` from HUD array publication. Its source brush asset pointer is `0x13`, leading to the read at `0x27`. Supported-executable disassembly and bounded Ghidra decompilation show that array resize destroys trailing destination rows before copying replacements. Raw row snapshots therefore cannot own nested TabData/brush/text/delegate arrays during shrink or reordering. `Context::array` now stages the source into a transient native root of the exact array TypeInfo before modifying the destination, then destroys that temporary with RAII. Persistent setup baselines and the hidden Store item retain typed owners; Hub filtering recaptures rows after inline edits. DataModelObject cloning also verifies its real native descriptor before reading its TypeInfo and payload. These are source-lifetime/descriptor corrections, not exception suppression.
+
+Offline schema and executable evidence: `../pulse-native-setup-contract-evidence.json`, `../reentry-match-panel-contract-evidence.json`, `../pulse-native-array-publication-evidence.json`, and `../pulse-arraypublish-native-functions.json`. Regression fixtures cover nested owners during shrink/reorder, deferred reopening, Store restore, Hub filtering, failed staging/publication, repeated teardown and flag/editor/waiting transitions. The approved pulse/artwork and checkpoint material archive remain unchanged. Native schema/automated checks do not establish the new controller callback, rendered phone panel, multiplayer invite policy or complete Deathrace gameplay; those require live testing. No computer-use or UI automation was performed.
+
+The final Release solution build succeeded (`../native-lobby-panel-20261011-build.log`). After rebuilding the final lifetime fixture, all **73 CTest checks passed** again (`../../reskate-v2.0.3-tests-verified.log`, 21.52 seconds), including the new Store/Hub ownership cases. Exact embedded-bundle verification passed (`../native-lobby-panel-20261011-embedded-check.log`); no artwork or pulse assets changed. The runtime and integration trees are compared by normalized source bytes in `../native-panel-placement-source-sync.json`.
+
+The native Allow Join and Invite controls remain present and retain their authored callbacks. A separate admission audit found that the custom match protocol currently checks session identity, phase and capacity but does not enforce the native Party Only choice or filter custom invite announcements by the native Invite choice. This limitation predates these crash/lifecycle changes. The selected controls therefore must not be presented as tested custom multiplayer privacy enforcement. Exact native ranges, formatter evidence and implementation entry points are recorded in `../reentry-native-admission-evidence.json` and `../native-policy-research/native-policy-and-race-lifecycle-evidence.json`.
+
+The installed test build launched successfully in PID 27844. Its launcher recorded DLL SHA-256 `5ed2bb259b9f3527a60d2c64fd5b912db6a53ae1dab4f7828d94d12525990f7c`. A read-only native-registry capture after world loading found all six private Deathrace gate/finish roots resident in domain 7, each with the expected native ObjectBlueprint ancestry. Evidence: `../native-panel-placement-live-assets-20261011.json`. This verifies residency; it does not prove visible placement, control input or finish scoring. A final lease-retirement correction follows this test build.
+
+## Continuation: native gates, HUD anchors and Details panel (11 October)
+
+The verified local CAS source can have an empty entity slot while its creation bus is valid. Checkpoint creation now resolves that bus only after validating the unique local human skater, context, owner and canonical blueprint. Gate reconciliation consumes existing dirty marks before rebuilding, preserves marks raised by Destroy callbacks during creation, and repairs any group with fewer or more than four mesh parts. The regression fixture reproduces the live empty source and callback-during-rebuild cases (37 checks).
+
+The native Details panel uses the current active StackIndex, retains the original page's complete Back action, and replaces/restores only its owned Content presenter. Quit requests that native Back navigation before retiring its lease. Editor HUD controls sit above the radial HUD; gameplay header anchors are restored on mode changes.
+
+The targeted archive SHA256 is 71edd1b63ddd7ef0313809d568a1659e243070ea633949954da001a293881d49. Repeated binary comparison verifies exactly three normal-gate palette payload changes; all 101 other resource payloads, finish gates, approved selector, artwork, pulse and isolated debris resources remain unchanged.
+
+Release solution build succeeded; all 73 CTest tests passed in work/continue-native-full-ctest.log. The built DLL embeds the exact 107811401-byte archive. Saved native page/shortcut evidence verifiers pass. These checks establish build and ownership contracts; they do not verify visible gates or the new custom Panel/Quit in-game. The exact Activities_OpenPause_Button graph only publishes activity-menu selection; native pause transition behavior still needs a manual test. Native ending leaderboard/showcase remains under implementation, and custom admission still does not enforce the native Allow Join/Invite selectors.
+
+Deathrace feedback follow-up: remove the redundant Start flag selector; rotate with D-pad left/right; resize the complete gate with up/down; save with Start; undo with Y. Three native start dumps faulted while a non-model asset was passed to the native DataModelObject loader, so the supported loader now rejects non-record assets before its unchecked TypeInfo reads and logs the offending asset. This is a diagnostic crash guard; it does not prove the panel or race starts correctly live. Release build and all 73 regression tests passed. The official Spot Battle ending was captured at selection 9 with two celebration models; the custom native ending bridge remains unfinished.
+
+Deathrace gameplay follow-up: live feedback confirms starting no longer crashes, but gates were waiting for the already accepted native flag at route point zero. Racers now begin at point one. Segment-plane interpolation accepts fast crossings between samples and retains the exact gate width/height check; the referee still rejects duplicates, skipped gates and expired clocks. The editor groups LT/RT, rotation and sizing pairs, uses X for Undo to match the native glyph, and separates controls from the Deathrace logo/title. Gameplay shows an individual clock and a compact middle-left native list with place suffixes, player names, time and the existing crown/rough row styling; it does not use the broken legacy score/profile bindings. Deathrace finish results reuse those valid time rows.
+
+The private native panel resolves records explicitly in Context's locked manager instead of the expression wrapper's TLS manager. Authored/runtime TypeInfo aliases require identical hashes, sizes, field order, offsets and recursively matched child schemas. Its player list uses native Label presenters matching their actual data. The upstream S.K.A.T.E. adapter retains the game's native activity rule and backend/menu flow; custom matches retire their setup registration and therefore still need a manual check of the native pause transition, shortcut and Quit. Full native ending celebration and multiplayer admission remain unfinished.
